    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hi, I'm working on the lobby specs for a new law firm office in London. It's a high-traffic area, so I need to compare polished concrete, luxury vinyl tile (LVT), and natural stone. Can you give me a breakdown of how they hold up regarding maintenance and long-term wear resistance? High-traffic is a big concern here.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For high-traffic law firm lobbies, polished concrete offers excellent durability and is relatively low-maintenance once sealed, though scuffs can be visible. Natural stone provides a luxurious, timeless look but requires periodic sealing and grouting maintenance to prevent staining and cracking. Luxury Vinyl Tile (LVT) is generally the easiest to maintain and very resistant to moisture, though extreme heavy foot traffic can potentially lead to wear in certain high-abrasion zones.",
      "source": "target",
