      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Over 5-10 years, the main concerns with polished concrete involve etching from acidic spills, like certain cleaning chemicals or drinks, which can dull the finish. Abrasion from constant traffic can also cause dulling or micro-scratches if the proper finishes aren't maintained. Improper curing or sealant application initially can also lead to premature dusting or fading of the polish.",
      "source": "target",
